> Which capability each operation asks of a driver. run.sh reads this to decide
> what a scenario needs, unions in the scenario's `# requires:` line, and judges
> a driver on the capabilities it declared: a scenario needing one it did not
> declare is UNREACHABLE, never a failure of a rule the driver never claimed.
>
>   <capability>  <operation ...>
>
> A token holding `=` names a key rather than an operation, and any operation
> line carrying a word that starts with it needs the capability too. An
> operation on no line here is a scenario the suite cannot classify, and the run
> stops before any driver is asked. A layer joins by adding its line.

store     submit claim renew progress release finish intent recall hold state orphans plant sleep watch next close
transfer  run runshared stage
wire      credential refuse allow src=http:
wanted    drop sweep
identity  ladder bench value ceiling caneve serve speak identify proof trusted check same traces claimed
